{{define "content"}}
<hgroup>
  <h1>Secrets: {{.RepoFullName}}</h1>
  <h2>Build environment variables for this repo</h2>
</hgroup>

<article role="alert" style="background:#fff3cd;border-color:#ffeeba">
  <strong>Plaintext storage warning.</strong>
  These secrets are stored unencrypted in the Hub database (Phase 10 limitation —
  see the project's <code>docs/specs/phase-10-repo-build-secrets.md</code> §3 decision 7).
  Encryption is planned for a later phase. Restrict <code>/admin</code> access and the
  Hub host filesystem accordingly.
</article>

{{if .SavedFlash}}
  <article role="alert" style="background:#d1e7dd;border-color:#badbcc">
    Saved.
    {{if or .AddedN .UpdatedN .RemovedN}}
      ({{.AddedN}} added, {{.UpdatedN}} updated, {{.RemovedN}} removed.)
    {{end}}
  </article>
{{end}}

{{if .ValidationError}}
  <article role="alert" style="background:#f8d7da;border-color:#f5c2c7">
    <strong>Validation error:</strong> {{.ValidationError}}
  </article>
{{end}}

{{if .Error}}
  <article role="alert">Error: {{.Error}}</article>
{{end}}

<form method="POST" action="/admin/repos/{{.OwnerSegment}}/{{.RepoSegment}}/secrets">
  <label for="raw">
    KEY=VALUE per line. Lines starting with <code>#</code> are comments and stripped.
    KEY must match <code>^[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*$</code>.
    Multi-line values are not supported (newlines escape to literal <code>\n</code> on serialize).
  </label>
  <textarea id="raw" name="raw" rows="14" placeholder="DATABASE_URL=postgres://app:pw@db:5432/app
API_KEY=sk-xxxxxxxxxxxx
FEATURE_FLAG=on"
>{{.RawText}}</textarea>
  <button type="submit">Save</button>
</form>

<section style="margin-top:2rem">
  <h3>Notes</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>Empty value <code>KEY=</code> is allowed and saved as an empty string.</li>
    <li>Removing all lines and saving deletes all secrets for this repo.</li>
    <li>Changes apply to the <strong>next</strong> JOB_ASSIGN (already-running builds are unaffected).</li>
    <li>The first <code>=</code> on each line is the separator — base64 padding (<code>==</code>) and JWT values are preserved.</li>
    <li>Inline <code>#</code> is preserved (e.g. <code>COLOR=#abcdef</code>) — only line-leading <code>#</code> is a comment.</li>
    <li>Trailing/leading spaces around the VALUE are <strong>preserved</strong> as written. The KEY is trimmed.</li>
    <li>The repo full name is normalized to lowercase on save and read (case-insensitive matching with GitHub payloads).</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Dockerfile build mode caveat.</strong>
      Secrets are written to <code>&lt;worktree&gt;/.env</code>, which <code>docker compose up</code> reads automatically.
      In <strong>Dockerfile mode</strong> (<code>docker build</code> + <code>docker run</code>), the <code>.env</code> file is
      <em>not</em> auto-injected. To use these secrets there, either <code>COPY .env /app/.env</code> in the Dockerfile and
      load it at runtime, or pass them as build args explicitly.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Existing <code>.env</code> in the repo will be overwritten</strong> on every JOB_ASSIGN
      where at least one secret is registered. If the repo ships its own default <code>.env</code> tracked in git,
      keys not present in the Hub UI will be lost from that worktree.
    </li>
  </ul>
</section>
{{end}}
